We are building a Structured Interactive Notes Engine based on extended Markdown.
Instead of plain text notes, the system supports:
Custom blocks (steps, commands, tasks, callouts, queries)
Structured parsing (Markdown → AST → JSON)
Dynamic rendering as UI components
Conditional logic (role/environment-based visibility)
Optional execution (run commands, store output)
PostgreSQL storage (TEXT + JSONB or block-based schema)
This transforms simple Markdown into a Documentation DSL (Domain-Specific Language) capable of powering interactive documentation, runbooks, and structured knowledge systems.
🛠 Available Tools
🔹 React (Frontend / Editor)
Best options:
Tiptap – Highly extensible block-based editor (recommended)
Slate – Fully customizable structured editor
Lexical – Modern performant editor
MDX – Markdown + React components
remark / rehype – Markdown parser with plugin support
Best choice for your need:
👉 Tiptap + custom block extensions
🔹 Python (Backend Parsing)
Python-Markdown – Supports custom extensions
Mistune – Fast Markdown parser
markdown-it-py – Extensible and modern
Best choice:
👉 markdown-it-py or Python-Markdown with custom extensions